WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:09.450
In 2015, Brazil began experiencing a
major public health crisis: a large

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:13.650
number of babies were being born of
microcephaly, a birth defect that results

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:17.880
in abnormally small head and
underdeveloped brain. At the same time,

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.439
researchers discovered that Zika virus
was spreading around the population. Zika

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:26.640
virus is spread by mosquitoes, and can
cause fever-like symptoms. Researchers

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:30.510
began to wonder: could Zika virus also
be responsible for the uptick in

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:34.800
microcephaly? You may have heard the
phrase "correlation does not equal

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.360
causation." This is a problem that plagued
epidemiologists when they were trying to

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.170
figure out what the symptoms of Zika
actually were. Zika and microcephaly

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:47.010
were occurring at the same time and in the same place, meaning that they were

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:51.300
"correlated". But it is possible that
microcephaly was being caused by

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:55.800
something completely unrelated to Zika--
in fact, during the outbreak in Brazil,

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.940
some people believed that chemicals, not
a virus, was causing the uptick in

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:04.080
microcephaly. In order to properly
understand whether Zika was causing

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:09.000
microcephaly epidemiologists engaged a
variety of methods they had to rule out

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.140
other causes, conduct "case controls"
comparing microcephaly within Zika

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:17.610
affected areas to non affected areas, and
monitor Zika-infected women during

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:22.460
pregnancy to determine if and when
microcephaly occurred during development.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:26.610
epidemiologists also tested the disease
on animal models and analyzed the

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:31.470
molecular mechanisms of the virus. In
2016 the World Health Organization

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:35.360
confirmed that there was scientific
consensus that Zika causes microcephaly.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.990
In addition to understanding the
symptoms of a disease, epidemiology

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:43.829
involves tracing the origin and route of
a disease to determine its evolution.

00:01:43.829 --> 00:01:48.119
How is it that microcephaly came to be a
symptom of Zika when it wasn't before?

00:01:48.119 --> 00:01:53.520
The Zika virus originated in the Zika
forest of Uganda where it started out as

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.640
a relatively mild disease. Its symptoms
were fever, rash, headache, and achiness.

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:02.759
Researchers discovered that it was
spread via the Aedes mosquito, and that it

00:02:02.759 --> 00:02:06.810
could infect both humans and monkeys.
Further research in Zika transmission in

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:11.610
humans showed that it could be sexually
transmitted as well. From the 1951 to

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:16.240
2006 Zika, was identified
fourteen separate times throughout Africa and

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.970
South Asia. Until 2007, however, there were no large-scale outbreaks. At this point,

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:23.800
there was an outbreak on the island of
Yap.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:28.450
The CDC conducted studies and collected
samples, and eventually determined that

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:34.540
almost 75% of the population had Zika. A
second epidemic occurred in 2013 in

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:38.800
French Polynesia. At this point,
epidemiologists noticed a new symptom

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:43.390
associated with Zika: Guilin Barre
symptom, an autoimmune disease that can

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:49.239
cause temporary paralysis. By 2014 zika
had arrived in brazil probably by plane.

00:02:49.239 --> 00:02:53.320
But microcephaly had never been a
symptom of Zika before, and people

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:56.920
outside of South America who contracted
Zika were not experiencing the same

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:01.810
abnormally high rates of microcephaly.
Epidemiologists developed a hypothesis

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:06.100
that there are two main strains of Zika
virus. An "African" lineage and an "Asian"

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:10.660
lineage. At some point, the "Asian" lineage
split off from the "African" lineage and

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:14.050
acquired the ability to cause
microcephaly through a mutation to the

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:18.400
virus's genome. Therefore, only
populations infected with the "Asian"

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:22.600
lineage of Zika would experience
microcephaly as a symptom of Zika while

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:27.370
those infected but the "African" lineage
would not. Microcephaly is a public

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:31.660
health crisis, once epidemiologists
confirmed that microcephaly is a symptom

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:37.269
of Zika, the epidemic was declared an
international emergency in 2015 leading

00:03:37.269 --> 00:03:41.769
to the influx of funds to help fight the
disease. Because Zika only causes

00:03:41.769 --> 00:03:45.940
microcephaly in unborn infants, it became
most important to protect pregnant

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:50.290
mothers from being infected with the
virus. In 2015, Brazil urged the

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:53.980
population to avoid pregnancy, and many
countries such as the United States

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:58.480
advised their citizens not to travel to
zika-infested countries while pregnant.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:02.680
Because Zika is spread by mosquitoes,
mosquito eradication efforts were also

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:06.720
effective mechanisms of reducing the
number of infected individuals

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:10.510
Additionally, various vaccines have been
in development since the crisis first

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:14.980
broke out. Hopefully, learning from the
Zika crisis, we will be more prepared for

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:20.910
not only the next Zika epidemic but also
any emerging disease.

